# AXON for Cursor

This project uses [AXON](https://github.com/atopwebtechnologies/axon) (Atop eXecution Orchestration Network) for spec-driven development.

## Project context

Always read `axon/index.md` first when starting AXON work. It links to product definition, guidelines, tech stack, workflow, code style guides, and active pathways.

## Available commands

Map user intent to the matching skill in `.cursor/skills/`:

| User says | Skill to read and follow |
| --- | --- |
| Initialize AXON / axon-initialize | `axon-initialize` |
| Craft a pathway / axon-craft | `axon-craft` |
| Immerse in pathway / axon-immerse | `axon-immerse` |
| Design frontend / axon-compose | `axon-compose` |
| Investigate progress / axon-investigate | `axon-investigate` |
| Inspect completed work / axon-inspect | `axon-inspect` |
| Revert pathway or task / axon-revert | `axon-revert` |

## Workflow

```text
Context → Craft → Immerse (↔ Compose) → Investigate → Inspect → Revert
```

- `axon-compose` activates automatically during `axon-immerse` when frontend work is detected.
- Pathway artifacts live in `axon/pathways/<pathway_id>/` (spec.md, plan.md, metadata.json).
- Follow `axon/workflow.md` and applicable files in `axon/code_styleguides/`.

## Cursor-specific notes

- Use the AskQuestion tool for structured single- or multiple-choice prompts when an AXON skill requests user input.
- Ask questions one at a time in text chat unless a native modal tool is available.
- After installing or updating AXON skills, suggest the user restart the Cursor agent session so new skills are picked up.
